{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31a4-70ff-ba8f-d428b8df4743","id":"01a1a62e-671f-77a5-92d6-23ab56986402","idempotency_key":"0a43d84ebde6065e840cc4a4688585d91c5203e7c5a3042ae9fb7c16516ded1a","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T10:50:21Z","payload":{"note":"Four of five. crates/ai/src/tournament.rs implements the three formats to the rules in 40-play-arena-ratings.md: Swiss with ceil(log2 n)+2 default rounds, no repeated pairings, a bye worth 1 that counts as a win, and standings ordered points -> Buchholz -> Sonneborn-Berger -> wins; a Swiss round refuses to start until the previous one has every result, which is what makes pairing depend on results rather than on completion order. Knockout is seeded with the top seeds taking first-round byes, and a drawn tie queues a colour-swapped rematch that is played before the bracket moves on - the better seed only advances if the replay is drawn too. Double round robin uses the circle method with every colour pairing occurring exactly once across the two cycles. 18 tests cover the tie-break chain (including Sonneborn-Berger scoring a beaten opponent in full and a drawn one in half), bye allocation without repeat byes, no-repeat Swiss pairings across rounds, the knockout rematch and its colour swap, and that a double round robin really plays all n*(n-1) ordered pairs. STILL OPEN: i-a95a (persistent queue, pause/resume/step, concurrency limits) - that is the runtime and storage half: a schema for tournaments/rounds/games and a runner that holds N games in flight, so it belongs with t-3a41 rather than here.","target":"t-a98f"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
